.TH OTLITE 1 "October 2026" "otlite 1.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
otlite \- install, run and update OSINT command line tools by name
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B otlite
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B otlite run
.I tool
.B \-\-
.RI [ prefix : value ...]
.RI [ tool\ arguments ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B otlite
installs open-source OSINT tools from pinned, tested versions, each into its
own Python virtualenv under
.IR ~/.otlite/tools ,
and runs them by name. Typed inputs such as
.B u:johndoe
or
.B d:example.com
are turned into each tool's own flags. Every run's output is saved under
.I ./results
with a JSON sidecar holding the command, timing, exit code and SHA-256.
.PP
otlite is the no-Docker edition of OTInstaller (https://otinstaller.com); the
.B ot
command is the containerised one, which installs signed packages from the registry. otlite was
called otinstaller until version 1.0: the OTINSTALLER_* environment variables are still read, and
the first run copies API keys and settings from ~/.otinstaller.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Create ~/.otlite, show the responsible-use notice and ask to accept it.
Use \fB\-\-yes\fR in scripts.
.TP
.B start
Pick starter packs (the bundled playbooks) and tools from checkbox lists, then accept the
notice, create the key file and install them in one go. \fB\-\-playbooks\fR and
\fB\-\-tools\fR take comma-separated names and pre-select them; \fB\-\-yes\fR installs
them without questions, \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR shows what would be installed, and
\fB\-\-keys\fR asks for the tools' API keys afterwards.
.TP
.BI install " tool" ...
Install tools. \fB\-\-all\fR installs every tool that needs no setup.
.TP
.BI run " tool " "\-\- " args
Run a tool. \fB\-\-all\fR runs every installed tool that takes the given typed input.
.TP
.BI auto " target"
Detect whether the target is an email, domain, URL or username and run the
matching installed tools.
.TP
.B list\fR, \fBsearch\fR, \fBinfo\fR, \fBexample
Browse the tool catalogue.
.TP
.B update\fR, \fBcheck\-updates
Bring installed tools to the versions this release pins.
.TP
.B remove
Remove tools.
.TP
.B playbook
Run or list playbooks.
.TP
.B extract\fR, \fBdiff
Pull indicators out of saved results, or compare two runs.
.TP
.B keys check
Show which API keys in ~/.otlite/.env each tool can use.
.TP
.B crash\-reports \fR[\fBon\fR|\fBoff\fR]
Show or change opt-in crash reports. They are off unless you turn them on.
.TP
.B doctor
Check Python, git, venv and the home directory.
.PP
Run \fBotlite \fIcommand\fB \-\-help\fR for the options of each command.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OTLITE_HOME
Use another directory instead of ~/.otlite. OTINSTALLER_HOME is read when it is unset.
.TP
.B OTLITE_RESULTS_DIR
Save results there instead of ./results.
.TP
.B DO_NOT_TRACK\fR, \fBOTLITE_CRASH_REPORTS=off
Never send crash reports.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.otlite/.env
API keys, one KEY=value per line, mode 600.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://otinstaller.com/docs/otlite and https://github.com/OTInstaller/otinstaller/tree/main/otlite
